d or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 11 00 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast lumpectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm irregular portion of tan yellow to pink  fibrofatty tissue  with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm tan white  unremarkable skin ellipse on the anterior aspect  There is a short stitch designating the anterior margin  a long stitch designating the lateral  and a bow tie designating the cephalad  The posterior aspect is inked black  the anterior blue  the lateral green and the medial yellow  The specimen is sequentially sectioned from inferior to cephalad to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm well circumscribed  gray white  gritty  firm mass  which comes to within   0 1cm from the posterior aspect  0 3cm from the anterior  0 5cm from the medial  2 1cm from the lateral  2 3cm from the cephalad  and 2 5cm from the inferior margin  The remaining uninvolved parenchyma is predominantly dense  white  unremarkable fibrous tissue  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE  A D  Entire mass  with the closest posterior margin in cassette A  E F  Uninvolved parenchyma  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node 1 2  count  750   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm tan yellow  fibrofatty tissue  After fat removal  two tan white nodules were identified that are entirely submitted in cassette G  The remainder of the specimen is entirely submitted in cassette H  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  tertiary sentinel node  count  114   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan yellow  fibrofatty tissue