hat is lined by a tan yellow to brown granular surface and fibrous tissue that is attached to the previously mentioned skin scar  The mass is 7cm  from the inferior resection margin  4 5cm  from the nearest superior resection margin and 11cm  from the medial resection margin  The rest of the breast tissue is composed of unremarkable adipose tissue and breast parenchyma  Section Code A  mass in relation to the nearest deep resection margin B  cavity in relation to skin scar C E  mass F  area around mass G H  representative section of unremarkable breast parenchyma The axillary tail is bisected to reveal eight tan brown and rubbery lymph nodes that range in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 5cm   entirely submitted in I L  Also received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number and  right additional axillary node content  is 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  tan  rubbery to slightly firm lymph node  entirely submitted in M  Also received separately in two containers  Labeled  left breast reduction 350 grams  are multiple fragments of skin and breast tissue measuring in aggregate of 15 x 10 x 7cm  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast tissue  representative sections submitted in N and O  Labeled  left breast 155 grams  are multiple fragments of breast tissue measuring 10 x 8 x 5 5cm  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal focal fibrosis and multiple tiny cysts that are filled with clear fluid  the rest of the breast parenchyma is unremarkable  Representative sections are submitted in P and Q  Resident  Essam Ahmed  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Lynn Arlene Weston  M D  James Warren May Jr   M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST PART B  RT AXILLARY CONTENTS PART C  LT BREAST TISSUE   report_end  , Unchecked.
