h determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 AUG 98 at 16 03 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast tumor  is a REMOVED_DATE x 4 x 3cm fragment of oriented fibroadipose tissue inked in green and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 1cm firm  tan white stellate mass present 1 1cm from the posterior margin  0 6cm from the anterior margin  and 0 7cm from the superior margin  Representative sections are submitted as follows  NOTE  The tumor mass is submitted enitirely in cassettes A through C  A  Tumor mass and posterior margin  B  Tumor mass and anterior margin  C  Tumor mass and superior margin  D  Representative sections of fibrofatty tissue surrounding tumor  E  Representative section of fatty breast tissue away from the lesion  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  in three parts  Labeled  final shaved margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm aggregate of small unremarkable fibrofatty fragments  submitted entirely in cassettes F I  Labeled  sentinel node   are two fatty fragments  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE in aggregate  The larger fragment contains two lymph nodes  each sectioned and submitted separately in cassettes J and K  The smaller fatty fragment has  lymphoid tissue and is sectioned entirely in L  Labeled  RT axillary contents   are two fatty fragments  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm in aggregate  with multiple unremarkable lymph nodes of up to 1 4cm  in cassettes M O  Gross Description by  RHONDA YANTISS  MD Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST MASS   CARCINOMA PRESENT MARGINS NEGATIVE  O R  R