ace with the stitch is inked black  and the opposite surface is inked blue  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm white  firm area on the surface opposite part of the stitch  of which a representative section is frozen as FX 1 and is now in Cassette H  Radial sections of the remainder of the specimen are submitted in Cassettes I K  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel lymph node   are two fragments of tan pink soft tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  which are bisected and entirely submitted in Cassette L  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  R axillary non sentinel lymph node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm fragment of tan pink  fatty soft tissue  which is bisected to reveal a single lymph node  submitted in Cassette M  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  anterior R breast   is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm fragment of red tan soft tissue  which is focally hemorrhagic and entirely submitted in Cassette N  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  R breast  inferior med post   is an irregular REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue  which is unoriented and contains no grossly identifiable lesion  The entire specimen is submitted in Cassettes O P  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  superior med post   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm irregular fragment of unoriented  fibroadipose tissue  with no grossly identifiable lesion  The entire specimen is submitted in Cassettes Q R  Resident  MELINDA J  FAN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST  ADDITIONAL LESION   INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  QUN DONG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert H