Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  20 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 10 42 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  RESIDUAL INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  WITH FOCAL LYMPHATIC PERMEATION BY TUMOR  MICROSCOPIC FOCUS OF ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  SCAR AND CHANGES CONSISTENT WITH PREVIOUS BIOPSY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The sampled resection margin appears free of tumor   RIGHT AXILLARY  LYMPH NODES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN MULTIPLE  ABOUT 15  LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 55                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two specimens  Labeled  Lumpectomy  breast cancer site  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm mass with an attached skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm that has a 4 1cm healed scar  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm hard  stellate  white mass intermixed with yellow chalky areas  The central portion of the stellate mass contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm dark brown elliptical focus  The mass is 0 4cm from its closest margin  Labeled  Right axillary node  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm mass of adipose tissue with intermixed lymph nodes  Dissection reveals multiple lymph nodes that are entirely submitted  Section Code  A D  representative sections of the mass  E  closest resection margin  F J  axillary lymph nodes  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART A  AXILLARY NODES  RIGHT  PART B  BREAST MASS  RIGHT    report_end  , Unchecked.
