pper outer quadrant  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   First mass  including the closest anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   First mass  including the closest posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   First mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Second mass  including the closest posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast tissue between the first and second mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodular fibrous area lateral to first mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Third mass  including the closest posterior margin  lower inner quadrant    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast tissue between the first and third mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the upper outer quadrant  Received in formalin  labeled  left axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE aggregate of tan pink fibrofatty tissue  which is sectioned to reveal 28 lymph nodes  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 3 2cm in greatest dimension and multiple soft tissue nodules  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 0 9cm  The lymph nodes and the soft tissue nodules are entirely submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node  serially sectioned   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node  trisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two intact lymph nodes and soft tissue nodules   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two bisected lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Eight intact lymph nodes and soft tissue nodules   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three bisected lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nine intact lymph nodes and soft tissue nodules  Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erbB 2 Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells focally show moderate  2   strong overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  HE