Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 03 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass  two lesions                                                                                       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  SUPERIOR LESION   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA   GRADE II III   PRESENT AT AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN   SEE NOTE  BREAST  LEFT  INFERIOR LESION   BIOPSY  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA RADIAL SCAR MICROCALCIFICATIONS NOTE  The carcinoma is 0 8cm in greatest dimension  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  No intraductal carcinoma is present in either specimen  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 27                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab in two parts  Labeled  Left breast mass  superior  A  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of fibrofatty tissue with a localizing wire  Sectioning reveals a 0 6cm in diameter  distinct  poorly defined  gritty  white mass  The mass is suspicious for carcinoma but too small to freeze  The mass is entirely submitted in cassettes A and B  the remainder is submitted entirely in C through E  Labeled  Left breast mass  inferior   2  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue with a localizing wire  Sectioning reveals fibroafatty breast parenchyma with no grossly suspicious area  No tissue is frozen  Submitted entirely in F through R  Resident  Michael Pins  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT SUPERIOR  A    GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS LESION  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT INFERIOR  2   NO AREAS GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  O R