tablished and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  888  to chromosome 17 signals  70  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  2 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL   2   EXCISION PART D  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART E  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART F  CRYOSTAT FROZEN SECTION  SLIDE ONLY  PART G  CRYOS , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 51 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU ADJACENT TO THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 06 58                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 16 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a localizing wire  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm ill defined firm gritty white mass extending through almost the entire length of the specimen and present at the inked margins  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  now submitted in cassette A  Note that a portion of the mass is submitted for research  The remainder of the specimen is submitted in its entirety in cassettes B   J  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FXDX  1  BREAST  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA PRESENT AT AN INKED SURFACE  O R  Resident  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
