Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 MAY 96 ACCESSIONED ON  30 MAY 96 at 11 04 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  30    GRADE 2 OF 3  REMOVED_DATE CM IN DIAMETER MEASURED FROM SLIDES  EXTENDING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  70    LOW GRADE  SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM TYPES  HARBORING ABUNDANT MICROCALCIFICATIONS  EXTENDING WELL AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE TUMOR  SPANNING A REGION REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION MEASURED FROM SLIDES  A FULL SECTION WIDTH   AND EXTENDING TO INKED MARGINS  NOTE  No lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 08                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 54 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm soft fatty tissue  which is inked and sectioned to reveal at least a 2 0cm in greatest dimension  ill defined  firm  white mass with a gritty cut surface focally abutting the inked surface  A representative section is frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  The remaining mass is entirely submitted in A through F  and representative sections of remainder is in G through J  Resident  FANG FANG  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA WITH FOCAL INVASION  O R  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST MASS  LEFT  , Unchecked.
