Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 90 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 90 at 00 00 CLINICAL DATA  Prior breast cancer  right  three years ago  New lump left  Rule out                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  EXCISION   1 INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  60    MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  PRESENT AT SEVERAL INKED MARGINS  AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  40    FOCALLY COMEDO TYPE  SEE NOTE   2 INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA  NOTE  Vascular invasion is not identified  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 90 at 15 02                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  A few tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 AUG 97 at 14 15 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab labeled  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fatty breast tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal white streaks and one very tiny nodule  0 5cm in diameter  The remainder of the parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  The specimen is too small for frozen  no frozen done  The nodule is submitted in A  The remainder submitted in B and C  Resident  Dennis Sgroi  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DX ONLY  BREAST LEFT  BIOPSY   A SMALL REMOVED_DATE CM FIRM NODULE TOO SMALL FOR FROZEN SECTION AND ER PURPOSES  ALL SUBMITTED FOR PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  DAVID WEISSMANN  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Britain Walton Nicholson  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
