Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 29 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  80    REMOVED_DATE CM  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  EXTENDING TO AN INKED MARGIN  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  20    COMEDO AND SOLID PATTERNS  NOTE  Lymphatic and blood vascular invasion is not identified  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 04                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 19     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 neu AS REPORTED BY IMPATH BREAST  LEFT   Fifteen percent of the tumor cells stain fro HER 2 neu  Unfavoarable   Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 MAY 98 at 13 10 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a 1 0cm in diameter nodule sectioned to reveal a 0 7cm diameter somewhat firm  tan  well defined nodule approaching a margin and suspicious for invasive carcinoma  A touch preparation is suggestive of carcinoma and a small piece frozen as frozen section  1 at Dr  Carter s request  Remainder entirely in A and B  frozen in C  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
