Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  05 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 11 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  1  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH FOCAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA  RADIAL SCAR  FIBROADENOMAS  NO RESIDUAL CARCINOMA IS IDENTIFIED  CHANGES CONSISTENT WITH RECENT BIOPSIES  2  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 18 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 17 12                                                                                     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     The attending surgeon inquired about the gross description of the of the axillary lymph nodes indicating two grossly positive nodes and the final diagnosis indicating all axillary nodes to be negative for tumor  All breast slides from this patients breast specimens   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   were reviewed  All of the final diagnoses were confirmed  The house office responsible for the gross description of the  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  specimen indicated that the gross involvement by tumor was based on pale white coloration of the nodes and a slight increase in firmness  To interpret these gross alterations as  positive for cancer  was an error in judgement  that was inadvertently not corrected in the final typing of the reports  Added by  Max L  Goodman  M D  Signed On  11 MAY 94 at 14 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen arrives fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and is a 490 gm  11 x 19 x 4cm modified radical mastectomy specimen  with a 19 x 7cm skin ellipse with a centrally placed areola and nipple with the areola 3 0cm from the superior skin ellipse margin and 1 2cm from the inferior skin ellipse margin  There are two recent incisions  tied closed with suture material  The first is radially oriented starting just lateral to the areola and is 2 0cm in length  The second is circumferentially oriented and is 2 0cm superior and lateral to the areola  The deep surface of the breast specimen consists of fascia with attached strips of muscle up to 0 5cm in thickness  There is an attached 10 x 5 x 2 3cm axillary tail  Underneath the lateral  radially oriented scar  is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm blood and clot filled biopsy cavity  biopsy cavity  A    Underneath the superior  lateral  circumferential skin incision is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm blood and clot filled biopsy cavity  biopsy cavity B   Biopsy cavity A is 1 4cm from the closest deep margin  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm area of firmness between biopsy cavities A and B  On the medial side of biopsy cavity A there is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  stellate  fibrous region which is located beneath the nipple  Cheesy  white material can be seen filling dilated ducts beneath the nipple  White  fibrous tendrils emanate from this area and extend to the inferior resection margin  Biopsy cavity B is 0 2cm from the closest deep resection margin  On the medial portion of biopsy cavity B is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  firm  stellate  tan white mass  region C  which is 2 0cm from the nearest deep margin and 1 1cm from the nearest superior margin  This region is just superior to the area described underneath the nipple  Sixteen axillary lymph nodes are identified  two are grossly positive  Section Code  A   deep margin  biopsy cavity A B D   inferior margins from area underneath nipple taken radially E   area between biopsy cavities A and B F G   representative area underneath nipple H   deep margin  radial biopsy cavity B I   representative area C J   closest extent of region C to superior margin K   representative area of breast from medial portion of mastectomy specimen L   nipple M R   axillary nodes Resident  James Kirby  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  Robert Carl Hagberg  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  20 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON  20 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 16 07 CLINICAL DATA  Known lobular carcinoma left breast  additional calcifications of left breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  WITH FOCAL LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  SEE TABLE  1  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA AND SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X 0 5cm  measured on the gross specimen  Lymphatic vessel invasion  Not identified  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  Invasive carcinoma extends to less than 0 2cm from the anterior margin of the specimen in one focus  Stains for receptors  Not indicated  NOTE  The carcinoma is near the first localization wire  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 07 35                                                                                     BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  A few tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 07 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of breast with two needle localized wires  a double knotted stitch at the superior margin and a single knot at the medial margin  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior in blue  posterior in black  medial in yellow and lateral in red  It sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a 0 4cm biopsy needle tract in the area of the wire and an adjacent REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm gritty ill defined area with retraction located approximately 1 0cm from the lateral  red  margin and 0 5cm from the anterior  blue  margin  There is an ill defined area of nodularity in the area of the second needle localization wire  No frozen done  The remaining breast tissue is grossly unremarkable  SECTION CODE  A  Firm area with closest anterior margin B  Firm area and closet lateral margin C E  Close lateral and posterior margin F H  Second nodular area near the second needle localized wire I J  Random sections of breast tisssue including lateral and posterior margin Resident  SOUHAD YOUNES  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  AREA SUSPICIOUS INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 17 CLINICAL DATA  Status post right mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  1 0 CM   GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SEE NOTE  2  MICROCALCIFICATION  NOTE  Greater than 95 per cent of the tumor is infiltrating  foci of in situ carcinoma apart from the main tumor are not identified  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is seen  The inked margins are negative for tumor  The gross intraoperative impression is confirmed  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 17 22                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a 6 x 3 x 2cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with accompanying x ray and wire in place  Specimen inked and bisected to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm firm  gray nodule suspcious for carcinoma  Surrounded by fat  not present at margin  Nodule too small for other assays  No frozen done  Discussed with surgeon  Section Code  A B  nodule  C D  nodule  E F  margin  G J  margin  Resident  James Kirby  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST LEFT EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
