Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 MAY 96 ACCESSIONED ON  24 MAY 96 at 08 42 CLINICAL DATA  59 year old woman with left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM AS MEASURED ON A GLASS SLIDE  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE III III   PRESENT AT SEVERAL INKED RESECTION MARGINS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  No definite blood vessel or lymphatic vessel invasion is identified  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  FOCAL  3  ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  29 MAY 96 at 12 26                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody 